// GHCN-D daily observations read from the Parquet by_station tree: 8 US stations (7 major airports
// plus NY Central Park), 427 objects / 19,964,198 bytes / 2,941,551 rows, two-level hive
// partitioning STATION=<id>/ELEMENT=<code>. The whole USW00* subtree left NOAA's active set in
// 2025-02 (data stops at 20250206) and has been byte-frozen since - the same pin basis the
// ghcnd-usw3 CSV corpus rests on. STATION and ELEMENT are path-derived columns, auto-detected from
// the key=value segments; DATE is a Parquet STRING coerced by a declared integer mapping so the
// answers line up with the CSV corpus.
//
// Every shape ships twice. The plain test reads the corpus as ONE dataset bound to a comma-list of
// the 8 station globs; the `...Multi` twin reads the identical rows as EIGHT datasets unioned by
// `FROM st_nyc, st_lax, ...`, exercising the leaf UnionAll and PushAggregateThroughUnionAll against
// real object storage. The two expected tables are identical by construction and that identity is
// enforced offline on `check` - a drift in either fails precommit, not the nightly leg.
//
// Deliberate divergences from ghcnd-usw3 (same observations, other encoding), asserted not hidden:
// Parquet stores M_FLAG/Q_FLAG as NULL where the CSV tree stores empty strings (q10); ELEMENT is a
// partition column here and a physical column there; ID == STATION on every row, so the CSV
// corpus's ID-based shapes are dropped rather than duplicated.
// Expected tables derived at authoring time by clickhouse local over the scratch copy of the same
// pinned objects.

// corpus: ghcnd-parquet-8st
// reference-variant: ghcnd-parquet-8st-s3-parquet-snappy-nested-hive
// pinned: 427 objects (8-station comma-list), 19964198 bytes, frozen since 2025-02-09
// oracle: clickhouse local 26.8.1.1309
// oracle-sql: SELECT count() FROM file('STATION=*/ELEMENT=*/*.parquet')
// oracle-run: 2026-08-25
// read-shape: aggregate
// max-rows: 1
q01_pqCountObservations
required_capability: dataset_in_from_command
dataset: ghcnd_parquet: "{{corpus}}"
FROM ghcnd_parquet | STATS count = COUNT(*);

count:long
2941551
;

