// corpus: ghcnd-parquet-8st
// reference-variant: ghcnd-parquet-8st-s3-parquet-snappy-nested-hive
// pinned: 427 objects (8-station comma-list), 19964198 bytes, frozen since 2025-02-09
// oracle: clickhouse local 26.8.1.1309
// oracle-sql: SELECT STATION, toInt32(DATE) AS DATE, ELEMENT, DATA_VALUE FROM file('STATION=*/ELEMENT=*/*.parquet') ORDER BY DATA_VALUE DESC, STATION ASC, DATE ASC, ELEMENT ASC LIMIT 10
// oracle-run: 2026-08-25
// read-shape: topn
// max-rows: 10
// note: explicit NULLS LAST: ES|QL sorts nulls first on a bare DESC. DATA_VALUE has no nulls here
// defect: multi-source row materialization dies with HTTP 500 UnsupportedOperationException [can't append non-null values to a null block]
// defect-variant: ghcnd-parquet-8st-s3-parquet-snappy-nested-hive
// defect-detail: SourceExtractors.materialize builds each column's block builder from the FIRST non-null source block across split ids; when that block is a ConstantNullBlock the builder is a ConstantNullBlock.Builder, and the next split carrying real values fails copyFrom. Unioning 8 datasets mixes splits whose per-column nullness differs, so the all-null block wins the race.
// defect-oracle: clickhouse local returns the 10 rows below; ES|QL returns HTTP 500
// defect-evidence: the single-source twin q13_pqTopValues passes with THIS EXACT expected table, so the rows and the expectation are not in question - only the multi-source plan is. The other 14 Multi twins pass; q13 is the only one that materializes raw row columns rather than aggregating.
// defect-found: 2026-08-25
// multi-source: the same rows through 8 datasets unioned by FROM; the expected table is identical to q13_pqTopValues by construction
q13_pqTopValuesMulti-Ignore
